# NestJS Services

- Applies to backend service trees under `services/` (API, crawler, workers, …)
- Frontend/Admin Next.js apps also match; prefer `nextjs-ui` guidance for UI files
- One deployable service per directory; no monoliths
- Hexagonal style: controllers → application services → repositories/ports
- Public HTTP under `/api/v1`; admin routes JWT + `RolesGuard`
- Queues via BullMQ + names from `@openeventhub/shared`
- Every service exposes `/health`, `/ready`, `/metrics`
- Prefer contract/unit tests that avoid Nest decorator/tsx pitfalls when needed
- Docs: `docs/API.md`, `docs/REST_ENDPOINTS.md`, `docs/COMMUNICATION.md`
